{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 50, :comments ["<b>And die on the mountain.</b> Meaning: reconcile yourself to die, for the Holy One, blessed be He, does not take the souls of His devout ones except with their consent. And His saying ״וְהֵאָסֵף אֶל עַמֶּיךָ״ is along the lines of what they said (Ketubot 104a), that the righteous go forth to receive the face of a righteous person; therefore HaShem said to him that he would be gathered to his people who come out to meet him." "<b>Further,</b> it may be explained along this line, that He comes to give three reasons for the death of the man of Elohim. And this is the measurement of the verse: ״וּמֻת״, and the reason ״בָּהָר״ — meaning, along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory (Sotah 14a): why was Moses buried on Mount Nevo? Because of the sin of Pe'or, for whenever Pe'or rears its head, it finds Moses opposite it and is subdued, as it says (Deuteronomy 34:6) ״וַיִּקְבֹּר אֹתוֹ בַּגַּיְא מוּל בֵּית פְּעוֹר״. Second reason — ״אֲשֶׁר אַתָּה עֹלֶה שָׁמָּה״, meaning, in order that he may attain the felicity that he attained through the intermediacy of awesome good deeds, which he cannot attain while he is still joined with the body, for he cannot attain that degree — and that is His saying ״אֲשֶׁר אַתָּה עֹלֶה שָׁמָּה״ — meaning, in the supernal world. Third — ״וְהֵאָסֵף אֶל עַמֶּיךָ״, along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory (Bemidbar Rabbah 19), on the verse (Deuteronomy 33:21) ״וַיֵּתֵא רָאשֵׁי עָם״ etc., that through the intermediacy of Moses the wilderness generation will merit, and they are reckoned as belonging to him, as it says (Exodus 32:7) ״רֵד כִּי שִׁחֵת עַמְּךָ״ — and that is His saying ״וְהֵאָסֵף אֶל״ — meaning, for the sake of your people, to bring them to the World to Come. And even though regarding Aharon too we find that it says similarly (Deuteronomy 35:29) ״וַיֵּאָסֶף אֶל עַמָיו״ — wherever there is room to expound, they expound."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {1 "The verse citation for Aharon's death is given as Deuteronomy 35:29, but Aharon's death is actually narrated in Numbers 33:38; this appears to be an error in the source text and is translated as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:56.110582686Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}